    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean i get that there are different sides, but it feels like a lot of the \"growth\" people talk about doesn't actually reach the average worker. if you look at the actual data on manufacturing jobs and wage stagnation, it seems pretty clear that these big trade deals just hollowed out the middle class. can you explain why someone would still argue it was a success when the working class clearly lost out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
